-- Passage wg11-argument-writing-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('d57fbe3c-2159-54a6-9e5b-b08e6e716cae', 'wg11-argument-writing-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$A Semester on Stage$q$, $q$(1) Brightwater High School requires one credit in visual art but none in the performing arts, such as theater, music or dance. (2) Brightwater should require every student to complete one semester in a performing art before graduation. (3) Performing in front of others builds the confidence to speak clearly under pressure, a skill that college interviews and most careers demand. (4) A three-year study at Merriton State University followed 600 high school students and found that those who took a theater or choir course reported less anxiety about public speaking than those who did not. (5) Ensemble work also teaches students to listen and adjust to others, since a choir or cast succeeds only when every member does.

(6) Some students and parents object that the schedule is already crowded, especially for students in advanced courses. (7) The requirement could be met through a semester course, a summer workshop or two seasons in an after-school production. (8) Others argue that shy students should not be forced onto a stage. (9) Performing arts courses include roles in lighting, sound, set design and stage management, so no student must perform alone to earn the credit.

(10) The arts make life better. (11) A single semester in the performing arts would build skills that students carry into every field, and flexible options make the requirement fair to all.$q$, 'draft')
