   $q$Sentence (10) is vague. Which revision best connects the discussion of objections to the conclusion?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some people enjoy music more than they enjoy sports or other activities.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Because both objections can be answered with flexible options, the case for the requirement remains strong.","is_correct":true},{"text":"However, these objections show that the requirement may be unfair after all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-claim"},{"text":"The arts make life better for everyone in almost every possible way.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because both objections can be answered with flexible options, the case for the requirement remains strong.$q$, $q$The correct revision sums up the responses in sentences (7) and (9) and leads into the conclusion in sentence (11). The choice beginning with "However" reverses the writer's position.$q$, 'draft', 'd57fbe3c-2159-54a6-9e5b-b08e6e716cae')
