insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('40bf1ce4-4a92-57e4-a905-9be352631461', 'wg11-argument-writing-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Real Dishes at Oakhurst$q$, $q$(1) Each school day, the Oakhurst High cafeteria throws away about 1,100 plastic trays, cups and utensils. (2) Oakhurst should replace disposable dishware with reusable trays, cups and utensils that are washed on site. (3) Disposable items fill roughly forty bags of trash daily, according to a two-week count by the school's environmental club. (4) The district also spends about $21,000 per year buying items that are used for a single meal. (5) Reusable dishware, by contrast, can last for several years with ordinary care.

(6) The main objection is that washing would require a commercial dishwasher and extra labor. (7) Oakhurst's kitchen already contains a dishwasher that was installed in 2009 but has sat unused since the switch to disposables. (8) A district facilities report estimates that repairing it and paying a part-time worker would cost about $16,000 a year. (9) This cost is about $5,000 less than current spending on disposables. (10) Others worry that students will not return trays and utensils. (11) Schools in the Wren Valley district solved this problem by placing return stations at each exit and assigning student volunteers to staff them during the first month.

(12) Plastic is bad. (13) Okay, so just switch to reusable stuff already.$q$, 'draft')
