   $q$Which change to sentence (5) would most strengthen the reasoning of the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Add a specific lifespan and yearly replacement cost for reusable items, so the cost comparison in sentences (8) and (9) is complete.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Remove it, because the lifespan of reusable dishware has nothing to do with the claim.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-relevance"},{"text":"Add that the writer personally prefers metal forks to plastic ones.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"anecdotal-preference"},{"text":"Replace it with a statement that disposable items look cheap and unattractive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"emotional-appeal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Add a specific lifespan and yearly replacement cost for reusable items, so the cost comparison in sentences (8) and (9) is complete.$q$, $q$The cost comparison leaves out the price of buying and replacing reusable items, so specific figures would close that gap in the reasoning. Lifespan is directly relevant to cost, so removing sentence (5) would weaken the argument.$q$, 'draft', '40bf1ce4-4a92-57e4-a905-9be352631461')
